### TiendaBox - Pruebas del recurso Order
### Ejecutar en orden. Crea su propio producto de prueba (owner) y su propio
### cliente de prueba, y reutiliza tokens/ids automaticamente.

@host = http://localhost:3000
@clienteEmail = order.test@example.com
@clientePassword = prueba123

### 1. Login owner -> 200 OK
# @name loginOwner
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@tiendabox.com",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 2. Crear categoria de prueba (owner) -> 201 Created
# @name createCategory
POST {{host}}/api/category
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Order Test Category {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 3. Crear marca de prueba (owner) -> 201 Created
# @name createBrand
POST {{host}}/api/brand
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Order Test Brand {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 4. Crear producto de prueba con stock (owner) -> 201 Created
# @name createProduct
POST {{host}}/api/product
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Producto para pedidos",
  "type": "stock",
  "price": 100,
  "stock": 20,
  "category_id": "{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}",
  "brand_id": "{{createBrand.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 5. Registrar cliente de prueba -> 201 Created
# Si ya existe de una corrida anterior, devuelve 409 (no afecta el caso 6).
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Order Test Cliente",
  "email": "{{clienteEmail}}",
  "password": "{{clientePassword}}"
}

### 6. Login cliente de prueba -> 200 OK
# @name loginCliente
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{clienteEmail}}",
  "password": "{{clientePassword}}"
}

### --- Crear pedidos ---

### 7. Crear pedido con retiro -> 201 Created
# @name createOrder
POST {{host}}/api/order
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "delivery_type": "retiro",
  "items": [
    { "product_id": "{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 8. Crear pedido con envio -> 201 Created
POST {{host}}/api/order
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "delivery_type": "envio",
  "delivery_address": "Av. Corrientes 1234, CABA",
  "items": [
    { "product_id": "{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 9. Crear pedido envio sin direccion -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{host}}/api/order
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "delivery_type": "envio",
  "items": [
    { "product_id": "{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 10. Crear pedido sin token -> 401 No autenticado
POST {{host}}/api/order
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "delivery_type": "retiro",
  "items": [
    { "product_id": "{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### --- Consultar pedidos ---

### 11. Ver mis pedidos (cliente) -> 200 OK
GET {{host}}/api/orders/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

### 12. Ver mis pedidos sin token -> 401 No autenticado
GET {{host}}/api/orders/mine

### 13. Ver todos los pedidos (owner) -> 200 OK
GET {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

### 14. Cliente intenta ver todos los pedidos -> 403 No autorizado
GET {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

### 15. Ver pedido por id, cualquier logueado -> 200 OK
GET {{host}}/api/order/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

### --- Cambiar estado (owner) ---

### 16. Avanzar a confirmado -> 200 OK
PUT {{host}}/api/order/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "confirmado"
}

### 17. Avanzar a en_preparacion -> 200 OK
PUT {{host}}/api/order/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "en_preparacion"
}

### 18. Saltar directo a entregado -> 400 Bad Request ("Transicion de estado no permitida")
PUT {{host}}/api/order/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "entregado"
}

### 19. Cliente intenta cambiar estado -> 403 No autorizado
PUT {{host}}/api/order/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "status": "confirmado"
}

### --- Cancelar (cliente) ---

### 20. Crear un segundo pedido para cancelar -> 201 Created
# @name createOrderToCancel
POST {{host}}/api/order
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "delivery_type": "retiro",
  "items": [
    { "product_id": "{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 21. Cancelar pedido pendiente -> 200 OK
PUT {{host}}/api/order/{{createOrderToCancel.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

### 22. Cancelar pedido que ya no esta pendiente -> 400 Bad Request ("Solo se puede cancelar un pedido pendiente")
# Usa el pedido del caso 7, que a esta altura ya esta en "en_preparacion".
PUT {{host}}/api/order/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}
